// they are what was drawn, to two decimals, as the scene tool printed
// them. Each render is named by the stage of the router that drew it and
// its scene: `v2-before` before the merge lanes were planned again,
// `v2b-after` and `v2c-after` two tries at that, `case5` and
// `case6-head` the router of their day, `group-slide` and
// `group-final` with merged ends grouped, `case5-head` a fix to that,
// `canon` in canonical order, `partner` with the routes kept off the
// legs of others past where they part from their partners, and `facing`
// with auto ends facing their networks. `ideal` is the layout judged
// best, drawn with waypoints and given sides. `legs` routes round the
// port legs of others, and `bundles` keeps, of the layouts it routes in
// several orders, the one whose partners run together furthest, with
// auto ends drawn toward the centers of their networks.

